WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.430
The Hunger Games did a lot of things right,
faithfully adapting Suzanne Collins' bestselling

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:11.080
books into a blockbuster franchise that launched
Jennifer Lawrence to worldwide superstar status.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.059
But as good as it was, it didn't quite do
everything right.

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:18.210
Here's a look at some dumb things everyone
ignores about The Hunger Games.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:19.780
Idiocracy

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.880
The basic concept of the Hunger Games takes
some suspension of disbelief to buy into,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.160
but even then, the politics don't really make
much sense.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.780
Think about this: the folks in the districts
do all the hard labor to keep the rich people

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:37.620
in the Capitol flush with food, and coal,
and amazing hair dyes.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.219
Considering they need the workers in the districts
to keep working, wouldn't it make way more

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:46.440
sense to actually, y'know, feed them enough
to do that work?

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.320
Plus, given how technologically advanced the
Capitol is, using just a little bit of that

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.949
know how to help automate things like coal
mining would significantly boost productivity

00:00:55.949 --> 00:00:59.590
while also raising quality of life and morale
in the districts.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:03.299
Acting like a bunch of evil jerks might be
fun, but it just doesn't make good business

00:01:03.299 --> 00:01:04.760
sense.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.230
Drinking games

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:10.830
When we first meet Haymitch, he's pretty much
a useless, snarky drunk with no interest in

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:14.570
helping Katniss and Peeta figure out how to
survive when the fighting begins.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:19.510
Then, the next morning, jerkface is gone and
has suddenly been replaced by a helpful, wise

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.850
mentor who whips the District 12 team into
shape.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:28.570
That change happens literally overnight, so…
maybe all Haymitch needed that whole time

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:30.120
was a good breakfast?

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:31.960
Coaching fail

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.111
Speaking of Haymitch, he's apparently the
smartest dude in the entire country, because

00:01:36.111 --> 00:01:40.490
when the games actually begin, the contestants
from every other district act like a bunch

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:41.490
of idiots.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:45.930
Haymitch's big piece of advice is to ignore
the supplies at the cornucopia and just run

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:50.730
for the woods, because it's going to be a
bloodbath as the others fight over the goodies.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:51.780
And it is!

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.600
It seems obvious, but apparently the mentors
in the other districts didn't think to pass

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.270
this nugget of wisdom along to their kids.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:08.340
Because sure enough, a bunch of them get creamed
in the first thirty seconds.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.840
Maybe their mentors were even drunker than
Haymitch?

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.150
Wait, no, that's impossible.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.090
It's well after breakfast by this point.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.310
Burn, baby, burn

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:21.200
A pivotal moment in the Hunger Games takes
place when Katniss is chased up a tree by

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.150
a pack of other contestants.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:27.610
After a halfhearted effort to kill her, Peeta
convinces them to just make a campfire and

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:31.720
wait for her to die of, like, old age or something.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.530
That turns out to be a bad plan, because through
a complete stroke of luck, Katniss finds a

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:42.340
conveniently placed hive full of genetically
modified bees, which she drops on their dumb

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.020
heads.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.160
"I think those are tracker jackers.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:44.880
Am I wrong?"

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:49.500
"Ohh… those things are very lethal."

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:50.500
"Mm.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.180
Very."

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:58.180
But...if those kids can make fire, why didn't
they just, y'know, set fire to the tree?

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.380
Trees are made of wood, right?

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.070
Even in the future?

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:05.900
And if the flames didn't get her, the smoke
probably would have, or at least forced her

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:09.020
to jump — which probably would've hurt her
pretty bad.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:12.240
Way to go, you dead dum-dums.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.480
Cake wars

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:17.780
Peeta may not be the most useful guy with
a weapon, but he sure is one hell of a painter.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:23.130
He shows off his incredible camouflage artistry
during training, and again uses it to go incognito

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:26.810
after suffering a pretty substantial sword
wound to the leg.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:32.500
We're told he picked up this rare and impressive
skill by … decorating cakes at the District

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.500
12 bakery.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.500
Really.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.840
"I, uh, I used to decorate the cakes down
at the bakery."

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:39.600
"Oh…"

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:45.040
So does that mean that the US Military should
be tapping the camouflage skills of Duff "Ace

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.469
of Cakes" Goldman?

00:03:46.469 --> 00:03:50.800
Should the Cake Boss be teaching courses to
army cadets at West Point about how to disguise

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:54.709
yourself as a giant, edible pink rose...for
combat reasons?

00:03:54.709 --> 00:03:58.710
Just how the hell does baking and decorating
cakes teach a kid how to go full-on mud-man?

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:01.599
Listen, Peeta, we're calling shenanigans.

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:05.710
The amount of effort and talent it would take
to create that spotless camouflage is a whole

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:09.940
lot more than you'd pick up by writing "Happy
Birthday, Here's a Coal Cake" a few times

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.230
a week with an icing squirter.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:16.989
Plus, since we're on the subject, how would
anyone in District 12, which is entirely made

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:19.940
up of starving coal miners have the cash to
get a cake?

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.299
Thanks for watching!

00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:24.440
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.710
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

